a="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/44l5t6CCIdjx2PcrqGsjWd/02f7d1e2b5ecaf1319f8ab2b45af8b7e/app-user_center-profile-trading_fee_tier.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/44l5t6CCIdjx2PcrqGsjWd/02f7d1e2b5ecaf1319f8ab2b45af8b7e/app-user_center-profile-trading_fee_tier.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/44l5t6CCIdjx2PcrqGsjWd/02f7d1e2b5ecaf1319f8ab2b45af8b7e/app-user_center-profile-trading_fee_tier.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="900" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/44l5t6CCIdjx2PcrqGsjWd/02f7d1e2b5ecaf1319f8ab2b45af8b7e/app-user_center-profile-trading_fee_tier.png" alt="CT-app-user center-profile-trading fee tier"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>Open trading fee tier page to view the trading fee details</i></p><h2 id="4-how-do-i-check-the-current-fee-rate-for-a-specific-pair-on-the-trading-page">4. How do I check the current fee rate for a specific pair on the trading page?</h2><p>You can go to our <span class="okui-hyperlink-var okui-hyperlink okui-hyperlink-accent okui-hyperlink-underline okui-hyperlink-md okui-hyperlink-muted index_hyperlink__f2YQn" data-testid="okd-hyperlink"><a href="/en-us/trade-spot/eth-usdt" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_self" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-hyperlink-text index_mutedLink__UPRKk">trading page</a></span> and search for the trading pairs that you want. You can find the fee rates of the current trading pair on <b>Fees</b> in the <b>Order placement panel</b>.</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-web-trading page-view trading fee tier level" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3WMUo7uEJg6wHmriK9DWnE/afb7f6b320c90ddc6a48a33b088ef852/web-trading_page-view_trading_fee_tier_level.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3WMUo7uEJg6wHmriK9DWnE/afb7f6b320c90ddc6a48a33b088ef852/web-trading_page-view_trading_fee_tier_level.png"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3WMUo7uEJg6wHmriK9DWnE/afb7f6b320c90ddc6a48a33b088ef852/web-trading_page-view_trading_fee_tier_level.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3WMUo7uEJg6wHmriK9DWnE/afb7f6b320c90ddc6a48a33b088ef852/web-trading_page-view_trading_fee_tier_level.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3WMUo7uEJg6wHmriK9DWnE/afb7f6b320c90ddc6a48a33b088ef852/web-trading_page-view_trading_fee_tier_level.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3WMUo7uEJg6wHmriK9DWnE/afb7f6b320c90ddc6a48a33b088ef852/web-trading_page-view_trading_fee_tier_level.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3WMUo7uEJg6wHmriK9DWnE/afb7f6b320c90ddc6a48a33b088ef852/web-trading_page-view_trading_fee_tier_level.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3WMUo7uEJg6wHmriK9DWnE/afb7f6b320c90ddc6a48a33b088ef852/web-trading_page-view_trading_fee_tier_level.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3WMUo7uEJg6wHmriK9DWnE/afb7f6b320c90ddc6a48a33b088ef852/web-trading_page-view_trading_fee_tier_level.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="664" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3WMUo7uEJg6wHmriK9DWnE/afb7f6b320c90ddc6a48a33b088ef852/web-trading_page-view_trading_fee_tier_level.png" alt="CT-web-trading page-view trading fee tier level"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>You can find the current maker and taker fee on our trading page</i></p><p>Alternatively, you can log in to your account on <span class="okui-hyperlink-var okui-hyperlink okui-hyperlink-accent okui-hyperlink-underline okui-hyperlink-md okui-hyperlink-muted index_hyperlink__f2YQn" data-testid="okd-hyperlink"><a href="/en-us/download" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_self" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-hyperlink-text index_mutedLink__UPRKk">our app</a></span> then go to <b>Trade</b>, and select <b>More</b> and <b>Fee rules</b> to find out the fee level and fee rate for the current pair.</p><p>You can also view your 30-day Spot/Futures/Options trading volume, as well as the asset holdings and trading volume required to upgrade to VIP.</p><p>Fee rates are shown per instrument, so the rate on a spot pair and the rate on a futures contract aren&#x27;t the same. To see futures fee rates, open a futures trading pair and check <b>Fees</b> in the order placement panel, or select <b>More </b>&gt;<b> Fee rules</b> from the futures trading page. The rates shown are the ones that currently apply to your own account.</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-app-trading-view trading fee info" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4yceW90ZnNhqGBU0HWoWoR/a34432c3981a027f3d84fd3e71af93e6/app-trading-view_trading_fee_info.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4yceW90ZnNhqGBU0HWoWoR/a34432c3981a027f3d84fd3e71af93e6/app-trading-view_trading_fee_info.png"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4yceW90ZnNhqGBU0HWoWoR/a34432c3981a027f3d84fd3e71af93e6/app-trading-view_trading_fee_info.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4yceW90ZnNhqGBU0HWoWoR/a34432c3981a027f3d84fd3e71af93e6/app-trading-view_trading_fee_info.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4yceW90ZnNhqGBU0HWoWoR/a34432c3981a027f3d84fd3e71af93e6/app-trading-view_trading_fee_info.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4yceW90ZnNhqGBU0HWoWoR/a34432c3981a027f3d84fd3e71af93e6/app-trading-view_trading_fee_info.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4yceW90ZnNhqGBU0HWoWoR/a34432c3981a027f3d84fd3e71af93e6/app-trading-view_trading_fee_info.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4yceW90ZnNhqGBU0HWoWoR/a34432c3981a027f3d84fd3e71af93e6/app-trading-view_trading_fee_info.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4yceW90ZnNhqGBU0HWoWoR/a34432c3981a027f3d84fd3e71af93e6/app-trading-view_trading_fee_info.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="1864" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4yceW90ZnNhqGBU0HWoWoR/a34432c3981a027f3d84fd3e71af93e6/app-trading-view_trading_fee_info.png" alt="CT-app-trading-view trading fee info"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>Select Fee rules to view more about your current fee tier and rules</i></p><h2 id="5-how-can-i-check-the-trading-fees-in-advance">5. How can I check the trading fees in advance?</h2><p>Before you place an order, the order placement panel shows the maker and taker fee rate that currently applies to you on that trading pair, so you can estimate the cost yourself: fee = fee rate × the amount of crypto bought or sold when the order is filled.</p><p>What can&#x27;t be shown in advance is the final fee amount. Your order can be filled as a maker or as a taker, it can be filled in several parts, and it can be filled at a price that differs from the price you saw when you placed it. All of this affects the fee. The exact fee charged is available as soon as the order is filled: go to Order history, select Details, and hover over Fee to see how it was calculated.</p><h2 id="6-how-are-trading-fees-paid-can-i-pay-them-separately">6. How are trading fees paid? Can I pay them separately?</h2><p>Trading fees are taken from the trade itself. There&#x27;s no separate fee balance, and there&#x27;s no option to pay a fee from a different currency or with a separate payment method.The currency your fee is charged in follows the trade, not a fixed fee currency. When you buy on the order book, the fee is charged in the crypto you bought, so you receive slightly less than the quantity you ordered. When you sell, the fee is charged on the proceeds of the sale. Which currency that is depends on the direction of the trade, the product you&#x27;re trading and the details of the fill, so read the fee line on the individual fill in your order history rather than assuming one fixed currency.For spot and margin trading, the fee is: fee rate × the amount of crypto bought or sold when the order is filled. This is also why a confirmation email that shows the quantity you ordered can differ slightly from the amount that arrives in your account: the amount in your account is the amount after the fee.</p><h2 id="7-why-is-the-amount-i-received-different-from-what-i-expected-is-the-spread-a-hidden-fee">7. Why is the amount I received different from what I expected? Is the spread a hidden fee?</h2><p>The maker and taker fees in this article apply to order book trading on Spot, margin and Futures. If you buy or sell through the express Buy/Sell flow, or through Convert, you&#x27;re quoted a single all-in price instead of a separate fee. The cost of those routes is built into the quoted price, which is why the price you&#x27;re quoted to buy an asset and the price you&#x27;re quoted to sell the same asset at the same moment aren&#x27;t the same. That difference is the spread, not a hidden fee.The same applies on the order book. The best available buy price and the best available sell price differ, and if your order is filled against several orders at different prices, your average fill price differs from the price at the top of the book. Where a trade also involves a currency conversion, the conversion rate applies on top.A fee shown as 0% means no maker or taker fee is charged on that pair. It doesn&#x27;t mean the amount you receive matches your estimate to the last decimal, because the fill price still varies. A change in the value of your holdings after the trade is a price movement, not a fee.</p><h2 id="8-does-okx-charge-any-other-trading-fees">8. Does OKX charge any other trading fees?</h2><p>For order book trading, the charges are the maker and taker fees described in this article. For futures, you may also pay funding fees, a forced liquidation fee charged at the taker rate of your current tier, and an expiry settlement fee of 0.01%. There&#x27;s no risk fee, no markup added on top of your maker or taker rate, and no other charge applied to a fill.We don&#x27;t charge you for opening an account or for keeping an account open. Deposits, withdrawals and card transactions are priced separately from trading fees, and any fee your own bank or payment provider charges is set by them, not by us.</p><h2 id="9-is-there-a-daily-limit-on-how-much-i-can-trade">9. Is there a daily limit on how much I can trade?</h2><p>Order book trading isn&#x27;t priced or capped by a daily fee allowance. If an order of yours is limited or rejected, that comes from the order and risk rules that apply to that instrument and to your account — for example, the maximum order size for the contract, or your position and margin limits. The order panel shows the limit that applies when you place the order, and the error message tells you which one you&#x27;ve hit.Limits you may have seen elsewhere aren&#x27;t the same thing: Convert has its own limits, and deposits and withdrawals have their own separate limits. Neither of them applies to your order book trading.</p><h2 id="10-how-can-i-upgrade-my-vip-level-and-reduce-trading-fees">10. How can I upgrade my VIP level and reduce trading fees?</h2><p>You can upgrade your trading fee level by increasing your asset volume or trading volume.</p><p>Based on trading volume, you&#x27;re divided into two levels: Regular and VIP. As a VIP user, you&#x27;ll be categorized  into levels based on asset volume and trading volume over the past 30 days. Your level determines the trading fees for the next trading day.</p><p>When calculating transaction fee levels, if the spot trading volume, total trading volume of perpetual and futures contracts (USDT perpetual contracts, USDT futures contracts, USDC perpetual contracts, USDC futures contracts, coin-margined perpetual contracts, and coin-margined futures contracts), options trading volume, spreads trading volume, and asset volume meet the conditions for different trading fee levels, then you will enjoy the highest trading fee discount among them.</p><p>For example, if your spot trading volume in the past 30 days is 10,000,000 USD (meeting VIP 2), your total trading volume of perpetual and futures contracts (USDT perpetual contracts, USDT futures contracts, USDC perpetual contracts, USDC futures contracts, coin-margined perpetual contracts, and coin-margined futures contracts) in the past 30 days is 200,000,000 USD (meeting VIP 3), your options trading volume in the past 30 days is 5,000,000 USD (meeting VIP 1), your spreads trading volume in the past 30 days is 150,000,000 USD (meeting VIP 2), and your asset size is 5,000,000 USD (meeting VIP 4), then you will enjoy a VIP 4 fee tier, and all tradings across all business lines are eligible for VIP 4 benefits.</p><p>For details on trading volume and asset size requirements, please refer to the <span class="okui-hyperlink-var okui-hyperlink okui-hyperlink-accent okui-hyperlink-underline okui-hyperlink-md okui-hyperlink-muted index_hyperlink__f2YQn" data-testid="okd-hyperlink"><a href="/en-us/fees" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_self" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-hyperlink-text index_mutedLink__UPRKk">Trading Fee Rules</a></span>.</p><h2 id="11-how-do-i-view-the-total-trading-fees-for-futures">11. How do I view the total trading fees for Futures?</h2><p>To view your total trading fees or total trading volume, download your trading history and calculate the totals manually. Add up all the <b>Fee</b> amounts to get your total trading fees, and add up all the <b>Quantity</b> amounts to get your total trading volume. Please note that different trading pairs may use different trading units — make sure to confirm the relevant unit when calculating.</p><h2 id="12-how-do-i-view-the-total-profitloss-for-futures">12. How do I view the total profit/loss for Futures?</h2><p>In the Futures Analysis tool, you can view your total PnL from <b>November 1, 2022 </b>onwards. You can filter by the last 7, 30, or 90 days, or view all time. The <b>All</b> range covers data from November 1, 2022 to present. To access the Futures Analysis tool, follow the path below:</p><p><b>On the app:</b></p><ul><li><p><b>Method 1:</b> on the Futures trading page, select <b>More</b> &gt; <b>Futures analysis</b> &gt; <b>Futures PnL</b></p></li><li><p><b>Method 2:</b> on the App homepage, select <b>Assets </b>&gt; Tap on the<b> tiny arrow</b> beside<b> 1Y PnL</b> &gt; Select <b>Futures PnL</b></p></li></ul><p><b>On the web:</b></p><ul><li><p>On the OKX website, go to <b>Assets </b>&gt; Select<b> Analysis</b> &gt; <b>Futures</b></p></li></ul><p>Futures analysis is a summary view. To see every trade you&#x27;ve made, go to <b>Trade</b> &gt; <b>Order history,</b> or download your full trading history from Order center.</p><h2 id="13-how-do-i-check-the-fees-for-my-historical-orders">13. How do I check the fees for my historical orders?</h2><p>You can find the fees for your historical orders on the web in the following sections:</p><ul><li><p>From <span class="okui-hyperlink-var okui-hyperlink okui-hyperlink-accent okui-hyperlink-underline okui-hyperlink-md okui-hyperlink-muted index_hyperlink__f2YQn" data-testid="okd-hyperlink"><a href="/en-us/trade-spot/eth-usdt" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_self" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-hyperlink-text index_mutedLink__UPRKk">Trading page &gt; Order history</a></span></p><ul><li><p>Go to our trading page and select <b>Order history</b>. You will see the amount of the fee applied.</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-web-trading history-view trading fee" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/7ADI6OhlLwqKO5Cq93ppkY/a28ecfaff257102c0477642273ee9051/web-trading_history-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/7ADI6OhlLwqKO5Cq93ppkY/a28ecfaff257102c0477642273ee9051/web-trading_history-view_trading_fee.png"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/7ADI6OhlLwqKO5Cq93ppkY/a28ecfaff257102c0477642273ee9051/web-trading_history-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/7ADI6OhlLwqKO5Cq93ppkY/a28ecfaff257102c0477642273ee9051/web-trading_history-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/7ADI6OhlLwqKO5Cq93ppkY/a28ecfaff257102c0477642273ee9051/web-trading_history-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/7ADI6OhlLwqKO5Cq93ppkY/a28ecfaff257102c0477642273ee9051/web-trading_history-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/7ADI6OhlLwqKO5Cq93ppkY/a28ecfaff257102c0477642273ee9051/web-trading_history-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/7ADI6OhlLwqKO5Cq93ppkY/a28ecfaff257102c0477642273ee9051/web-trading_history-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/7ADI6OhlLwqKO5Cq93ppkY/a28ecfaff257102c0477642273ee9051/web-trading_history-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="888" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/7ADI6OhlLwqKO5Cq93ppkY/a28ecfaff257102c0477642273ee9051/web-trading_history-view_trading_fee.png" alt="CT-web-trading history-view trading fee"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>Find the fee amount in your order history</i></p></li><li><p>If you would like to check out how the fee is calculated, you can select <b>Details</b> and hover over the <b>Fee</b>.</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-web-trading-transaction details-view trading rules" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/4SkqclPH0BExkZ7af5uliY/0e5250b0f1504c8aca2b933042dddeb9/web-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/to