p/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/23TyoTV9WtCqxKxNtXPud9/4ece8dace3a5a1cb5e9a9116190a73fc/web-asset_dropdown-Order_center.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/23TyoTV9WtCqxKxNtXPud9/4ece8dace3a5a1cb5e9a9116190a73fc/web-asset_dropdown-Order_center.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="664" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/23TyoTV9WtCqxKxNtXPud9/4ece8dace3a5a1cb5e9a9116190a73fc/web-asset_dropdown-Order_center.png" alt="CT-web-asset dropdown-Order center"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>Opening Order center page</i></p></li><li><p>If you would like to check out how the fee is calculated, you can select <b>Details</b> and hover over the <b>Fee</b>.</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-web-order center-transaction details-view trading rules" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/69X08BNDlwthAx0zeois2E/2ed4b5a2fbdfd42546eb1bc3a05039d7/web-order_center-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/69X08BNDlwthAx0zeois2E/2ed4b5a2fbdfd42546eb1bc3a05039d7/web-order_center-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/69X08BNDlwthAx0zeois2E/2ed4b5a2fbdfd42546eb1bc3a05039d7/web-order_center-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/69X08BNDlwthAx0zeois2E/2ed4b5a2fbdfd42546eb1bc3a05039d7/web-order_center-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/69X08BNDlwthAx0zeois2E/2ed4b5a2fbdfd42546eb1bc3a05039d7/web-order_center-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/69X08BNDlwthAx0zeois2E/2ed4b5a2fbdfd42546eb1bc3a05039d7/web-order_center-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/69X08BNDlwthAx0zeois2E/2ed4b5a2fbdfd42546eb1bc3a05039d7/web-order_center-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/69X08BNDlwthAx0zeois2E/2ed4b5a2fbdfd42546eb1bc3a05039d7/web-order_center-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/69X08BNDlwthAx0zeois2E/2ed4b5a2fbdfd42546eb1bc3a05039d7/web-order_center-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="664" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/69X08BNDlwthAx0zeois2E/2ed4b5a2fbdfd42546eb1bc3a05039d7/web-order_center-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png" alt="CT-web-order center-transaction details-view trading rules"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>Select details to find out how the fee is calculated</i></p></li></ul></li></ul><p>Alternatively, you can find the fees for your historical orders in <span class="okui-hyperlink-var okui-hyperlink okui-hyperlink-accent okui-hyperlink-underline okui-hyperlink-md okui-hyperlink-muted index_hyperlink__f2YQn" data-testid="okd-hyperlink"><a href="/en-us/download" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_self" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-hyperlink-text index_mutedLink__UPRKk">our app</a></span> by going to <b>Trade</b>, selecting <b>My trades</b>, and find <b>Order history</b>.</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-app-trading-view transaction history" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3NiNSYBkUc5fQ4PwjXJydN/c77858b3135b2f202706d04fc8757cd8/app-trading-view_transaction_history.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3NiNSYBkUc5fQ4PwjXJydN/c77858b3135b2f202706d04fc8757cd8/app-trading-view_transaction_history.png"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3NiNSYBkUc5fQ4PwjXJydN/c77858b3135b2f202706d04fc8757cd8/app-trading-view_transaction_history.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3NiNSYBkUc5fQ4PwjXJydN/c77858b3135b2f202706d04fc8757cd8/app-trading-view_transaction_history.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3NiNSYBkUc5fQ4PwjXJydN/c77858b3135b2f202706d04fc8757cd8/app-trading-view_transaction_history.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3NiNSYBkUc5fQ4PwjXJydN/c77858b3135b2f202706d04fc8757cd8/app-trading-view_transaction_history.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3NiNSYBkUc5fQ4PwjXJydN/c77858b3135b2f202706d04fc8757cd8/app-trading-view_transaction_history.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3NiNSYBkUc5fQ4PwjXJydN/c77858b3135b2f202706d04fc8757cd8/app-trading-view_transaction_history.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3NiNSYBkUc5fQ4PwjXJydN/c77858b3135b2f202706d04fc8757cd8/app-trading-view_transaction_history.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="900" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/3NiNSYBkUc5fQ4PwjXJydN/c77858b3135b2f202706d04fc8757cd8/app-trading-view_transaction_history.png" alt="CT-app-trading-view transaction history"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>Open your transaction history page</i></p><p>Select the transaction history that you want to view, and you will find the amount of the fee applied at <b>Fill details</b>.</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-app-trading-transaction details-view trading fee" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/6N5p2ngHMnMsTxFKelqcAO/a4c6fb5cba6fba838b9cca1e926926ef/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/6N5p2ngHMnMsTxFKelqcAO/a4c6fb5cba6fba838b9cca1e926926ef/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_fee.png"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/6N5p2ngHMnMsTxFKelqcAO/a4c6fb5cba6fba838b9cca1e926926ef/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/6N5p2ngHMnMsTxFKelqcAO/a4c6fb5cba6fba838b9cca1e926926ef/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/6N5p2ngHMnMsTxFKelqcAO/a4c6fb5cba6fba838b9cca1e926926ef/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/6N5p2ngHMnMsTxFKelqcAO/a4c6fb5cba6fba838b9cca1e926926ef/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/6N5p2ngHMnMsTxFKelqcAO/a4c6fb5cba6fba838b9cca1e926926ef/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/6N5p2ngHMnMsTxFKelqcAO/a4c6fb5cba6fba838b9cca1e926926ef/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/6N5p2ngHMnMsTxFKelqcAO/a4c6fb5cba6fba838b9cca1e926926ef/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="900" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/6N5p2ngHMnMsTxFKelqcAO/a4c6fb5cba6fba838b9cca1e926926ef/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_fee.png" alt="CT-app-trading-transaction details-view trading fee"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>Find the fee that has been applied on the past transaction</i></p><p>If you would like to check out how the fee is calculated, you can select the fee amount and you will be able to view the fee details.</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-app-trading-transaction details-view trading rules" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/5aP2ncZc1oYDE64sTmRpbf/47fee5b4d416325dae7db661f7eac8e4/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/5aP2ncZc1oYDE64sTmRpbf/47fee5b4d416325dae7db661f7eac8e4/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/5aP2ncZc1oYDE64sTmRpbf/47fee5b4d416325dae7db661f7eac8e4/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/5aP2ncZc1oYDE64sTmRpbf/47fee5b4d416325dae7db661f7eac8e4/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/5aP2ncZc1oYDE64sTmRpbf/47fee5b4d416325dae7db661f7eac8e4/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/5aP2ncZc1oYDE64sTmRpbf/47fee5b4d416325dae7db661f7eac8e4/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/5aP2ncZc1oYDE64sTmRpbf/47fee5b4d416325dae7db661f7eac8e4/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/5aP2ncZc1oYDE64sTmRpbf/47fee5b4d416325dae7db661f7eac8e4/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/5aP2ncZc1oYDE64sTmRpbf/47fee5b4d416325dae7db661f7eac8e4/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="900" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/5aP2ncZc1oYDE64sTmRpbf/47fee5b4d416325dae7db661f7eac8e4/app-trading-transaction_details-view_trading_rules.png" alt="CT-app-trading-transaction details-view trading rules"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>View how your trading fee is calculated</i></p><h2 id="14-how-is-my-trading-fee-level-determined">14. How is my trading fee level determined?</h2><p>You can enhance your fee levels by increasing asset amount or trading volume.</p><p>Based on trading volume, users are categorized into regular and VIP levels. VIP users are classified based on the asset amount or trading volume over the past 30 days. Different levels determine the trading fees for the next trading day.</p><p>When calculating the fee level, if your spot trading volume, total volume of perpetual and expiry futures (USDT perpetual futures, USDT expiry futures, USDC perpetual futures, USDC expiry futures, crypto-margined perpetual futures, and crypto-margined expiry futures), option trading volume, spreads trading volume, and the asset amount, meet the conditions for different fee levels, you will enjoy the highest level of fee benefits, i.e., the most favorable fee rate.</p><h2 id="15-how-is-the-trading-fee-calculated">15. How is the trading fee calculated?</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><tbody><tr><td><p><b>Instruments</b></p></td><td><p><b>Calculation formulas of trading fees</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Spot/Margin</p></td><td><p><b>Trading fee of Spot/Margin = Fee rate × Amount of bought or sold crypto when order filled.</b></p><p><b>Charge rule of crypto: Fee = Fee rate × Amount of bought crypto when order was filled;</b></p><p>Take BTC/USDT spot as an example, assuming the current price of BTC is 20,000 USDT;</p><p>Trader A (Maker fee: 0.08%; Taker fee: 0.1%) bought 1 BTC at market price, and became a taker of this trade, so the Trading fee = 0.1% × 1 = 0.001 BTC, and A will receive 0.999 BTC after fee deducted;</p><p>Trader A sold 1 BTC at limit price, and received 20,000 USDT. Trader A became a maker of this trade, so the Trading fee = 0.08% × 20,000 = 16 USDT, and A will receive 19,984 USDT after fee deducted.</p><p></p><p><b>Trading fee rebate rule: Fee = Fee rate × Amount of sold crypto when order was filled;</b></p><p>Take BTC/USDT spot as an example, assuming the current price of BTC is 20,000 USDT;</p><p>Trader A (Maker fee: -0.002%; Taker fee: 0.025%) sold 1 BTC at limit price, and became a maker of this trade, so the Trading fee rebated to A = 0.002% × 1 = 0.00002 BTC;</p><p>Trader A bought 1 BTC with a limit order, and received 20,000 USDT. Trader A became a maker of this trade, so the Trading fee rebated to A = 0.002% × 1 × 20,000 = 0.4 USDT;</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Futures</p></td><td><p><b>Trading fee of USDT-margined and USDC-margined perpetual and expiry futures = Fee rate × (Number of contracts × Contract Multiplier × Contract size × Fill price).</b></p><p><b>Charge rule: Trading fee of USDT-margined perpetual futures is settled in USDT and is charged when the order is filled;</b></p><p>Take BTCUSDT perpetual futures (Contract size is 0.01 BTC, Contract Multiplier is 1) as an example, assuming the current price of BTC is 20,000 USDT;</p><p>Trader A (Maker fee: 0.02%; Taker fee: 0.05%) bought/sold 100 contracts (1 BTC) at market price with 10x leverage, and used 2,000 USDT (0.1 BTC) as margin. Trader A became a taker of this trade, so the Trading fee = 0.05% × (100 × 1 × 0.01 × 20,000) = 10 USDT;</p><p>Trader A bought/sold 100 contracts (1 BTC) at limit price with 10x leverage, and used 2,000 USDT (0.1 BTC) as margin. Trader A became a maker of this trade, so the Trading fee = 0.02% × (100 × 1 × 0.01 × 20,000) = 4 USDT.</p><p></p><p><b>Trading fee of Crypto-margined perpetual and expiry futures = Fee rate × (Number of contracts × Contract Multiplier × Face value per contract / Fill price).</b></p><p><b>Charge rule: Trading fee for Crypto-margined perpetual and expiry futures is settled in the traded crypto and is charged when the order is filled;</b></p><p>Take BTCUSD perpetual futures (Contract size is 100 USD, Contract Multiplier is 1) as an example, assuming the market price of BTC is 20,000 USD.</p><p>Trader A (Maker fee: 0.02%; Taker fee: 0.05%) bought/sold 100 contracts (10,000 USD) at market price with 10x leverage, and uses 0.05 BTC (1,000 USD) as margin. If Trader A is the taker of this trade, the trading fee = 0.05% × (100 × 1 × 100 / 20,000) = 0.00025 BTC;</p><p>Trader A bought/sold 100 contracts (10,000 USD) at limit price with 10x leverage, and uses 0.05 BTC (1,000 USD) as a margin. If Trader A is the maker of this trade, the trading fee = 0.02% × (100 × 1 × 100 / 20,000) = 0.0001 BTC.</p><p></p><p><b>Forced liquidation fee: Calculated according to the taker fee of user’s current tier level.</b></p><p><b></b></p><p><b>Expiry settlement fee: 0.01% for all users regardless of tier level.</b></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Options</p></td><td><p><b>Trading fee of options = Min(Fee rate × Contract</b> <b>Multiplier × Contract size × Number of contracts, 7% × Option premium × Contract Multiplier × Contract size × Number of contracts)</b></p><p>Take BTCUSD options (Contract Multiplier is 0.01, Contract size is 1 BTC, Option premium is 0.05 BTC) as an example.</p><p>Trader A (Maker fee: 0.02%; Taker fee: 0.03%) bought 100 contracts of call options (notional is 1 BTC):</p><p>If trader A is the taker when order filled, so the Trading fee = Min(0.03% × 0.01 × 1 × 100, 7% × 0.05 × 0.01 × 1 × 100) = 0.0003 BTC;</p><p>If trader A is the maker when order filled, so the Trading fee = Min(0.02% × 0.01 × 1 × 100, 7% × 0.05 × 0.01 × 1 × 100) = 0.0002 BTC.</p><p></p><p><b>Exercise fee = Min(0.02% × Contract Multiplier × Contract size × Number of contracts, User’s taker fee rate × Contract Multiplier × Contract size × Number of contracts, 7% × Settlement value × Contract Multiplier × Contract size × Number of contracts)</b></p><p>Day options don’t have an exercise fee. Day options are options that don’t expire on Fridays. Only applicable to exercised options. Doesn’t apply to unexercised options.</p><p></p><p><b>Forced liquidation fee = Min(User’s taker fee rate × Contract Multiplier × Contract size × Number of contracts, 7% × mark price × Contract Multiplier × Contract size × Number of contracts)</b></p><p>Options combo trades on RFQ can enjoy up to 50% discount on fees!</p><p>For each underlying asset, trading fees are charged on legs from the side (buy or sell) with the higher notional.</p><p>Only legs that incur a trading fee are counted towards the 30-day trading volume of the corresponding instrument.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Spreads</p></td><td><p>Each instrument’s fee rate is 50% off from its classic order book rate as shown in the fee tier.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>For more details about trading fee structure, please visit <span class="okui-hyperlink-var okui-hyperlink okui-hyperlink-accent okui-hyperlink-underline okui-hyperlink-md okui-hyperlink-muted index_hyperlink__f2YQn" data-testid="okd-hyperlink"><a href="/en-us/fees" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_self" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-hyperlink-text index_mutedLink__UPRKk">here</a></span>.</p><h2 id="16-whats-the-difference-between-futures-opening-and-closing-fees">16. What’s the difference between futures opening and closing fees?</h2><p>Fees are charged when an order is executed. There is no difference between the fees for opening or closing positions. Fees are collected based on the executed size of the order, corresponding to either the taker or maker fee.</p><h2 id="17-are-fees-charged-for-liquidation">17. Are fees charged for liquidation?</h2><p>Forced liquidation fees are charged according to the taker fee rate of your current level.</p><h2 id="18-why-is-there-a-discrepancy-between-the-profit-when-holding-a-position-and-after-closing-it">18. Why is there a discrepancy between the profit when holding a position and after closing it?</h2><p>For futures and options trading, the realized profit after closing a position is the net profit after deducting trading and funding fees. The difference between the profit when holding and after closing a position is due to these trading and funding fees.</p><p>For example, in a BTCUSDT perpetual contract, if your current position value is 20,000 USDT with a floating profit of 15 USDT, the opened trading fee is -4 USDT, the closed trading fee is -5 USDT, and the funding fee is -1 USDT. After closing the position, your realized profit will be 5 USDT (= 15 USDT – 4 USDT – 5 USDT – 1 USDT).</p><p>For margin trading, only the closed profit is recorded, without realized profit, so the profit when holding and after closing the position remains consistent.</p><p>Fees aren&#x27;t the only reason your result can differ from what you expected:</p><ul><li><p>Futures trading fees are calculated on the size of your position, not on the margin you put up. If you open a 20,000 USDT position at 10x leverage with 2,000 USDT of margin, your fee rate is applied to the 20,000 USDT position value, not to the 2,000 USDT of margin. The higher your leverage, the larger the amount your fee rate is applied to.</p></li><li><p>A stop-loss or take-profit order isn&#x27;t on the order book until it&#x27;s triggered. Once it&#x27;s triggered, your order is submitted at the order price you preset when you created it, and if that&#x27;s the market price it&#x27;s filled at the best price then available. In a fast-moving or less liquid market, that price can be worse than your trigger price, and the difference shows up as a larger loss than the one you calculated from your trigger price.</p></li><li><p>Account-level profit figures include the unrealized profit and loss on positions that are still open, so adding up only your closed trades gives you a different number.</p></li></ul><h2 id="19-why-are-the-profits-from-order-history-and-position-history-inconsistent">19. Why are the profits from Order history and Position history inconsistent?</h2><p>For <b>futures and options trading</b>, the realized profits in <b>Position history</b> include closed profits, funding fees, and trading fees, whereas the profits from <b>Order history </b>only include closed profits. For example, after closing the following position:</p><p>From the <b>Order history </b>list, the opened and closed trading fees are both -0.03 USDT, and the closed profit is +0.46 USDT.</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-web-futures and options trading-realized PnL and fee" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/34RK3tqtGjtOJrQJkBqoY9/7851976c85ef4e4fb451e2019ee9b157/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_and_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/34RK3tqtGjtOJrQJkBqoY9/7851976c85ef4e4fb451e2019ee9b157/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_and_fee.png"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/34RK3tqtGjtOJrQJkBqoY9/7851976c85ef4e4fb451e2019ee9b157/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_and_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/34RK3tqtGjtOJrQJkBqoY9/7851976c85ef4e4fb451e2019ee9b157/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_and_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/34RK3tqtGjtOJrQJkBqoY9/7851976c85ef4e4fb451e2019ee9b157/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_and_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/34RK3tqtGjtOJrQJkBqoY9/7851976c85ef4e4fb451e2019ee9b157/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_and_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/34RK3tqtGjtOJrQJkBqoY9/7851976c85ef4e4fb451e2019ee9b157/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_and_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/34RK3tqtGjtOJrQJkBqoY9/7851976c85ef4e4fb451e2019ee9b157/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_and_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/34RK3tqtGjtOJrQJkBqoY9/7851976c85ef4e4fb451e2019ee9b157/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_and_fee.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="254" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/34RK3tqtGjtOJrQJkBqoY9/7851976c85ef4e4fb451e2019ee9b157/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_and_fee.png" alt="CT-web-futures and options trading-realized PnL and fee"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>Find the trading fees of your order history</i></p><p>From the <b>Position history</b> list, the realized profit for this position includes a closed profit of +0.46 USDT. The funding fee is 0, and the trading fee is -0.06 USDT (= Opened trading fee + Closed trading fee), so the total realized profit is +0.40 USDT (= Closed profit + Funding fee + Trading fee).</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-web-futures and options trading-realized PnL details" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/2uRCz9lzGjCg7ZUUbdJHWB/ec4e6d6bef5278702c38fd2e3ada74e5/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/2uRCz9lzGjCg7ZUUbdJHWB/ec4e6d6bef5278702c38fd2e3ada74e5/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_details.png"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/2uRCz9lzGjCg7ZUUbdJHWB/ec4e6d6bef5278702c38fd2e3ada74e5/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/2uRCz9lzGjCg7ZUUbdJHWB/ec4e6d6bef5278702c38fd2e3ada74e5/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/2uRCz9lzGjCg7ZUUbdJHWB/ec4e6d6bef5278702c38fd2e3ada74e5/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/2uRCz9lzGjCg7ZUUbdJHWB/ec4e6d6bef5278702c38fd2e3ada74e5/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/2uRCz9lzGjCg7ZUUbdJHWB/ec4e6d6bef5278702c38fd2e3ada74e5/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/2uRCz9lzGjCg7ZUUbdJHWB/ec4e6d6bef5278702c38fd2e3ada74e5/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/2uRCz9lzGjCg7ZUUbdJHWB/ec4e6d6bef5278702c38fd2e3ada74e5/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="400" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/2uRCz9lzGjCg7ZUUbdJHWB/ec4e6d6bef5278702c38fd2e3ada74e5/web-futures_and_options_trading-realized_PnL_details.png" alt="CT-web-futures and options trading-realized PnL details"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>Find the realized PnL details by hovering over to PNL%</i></p><p>For <b>margin trading</b>, only the closed PnL is recorded, without realized profit, hence the earnings in <b>Order history</b> and <b>Position history</b> are consistent.</p><figure class="assetContainer"><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="undefined CT-web-margin trading-realized PnL details" data-testid="okd-image-viewer" class="okui-plain-button okui-image-viewer index_container__iJVBI"><picture class="okui-picture okui-picture-font"><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/GUCBY2ITkAgErQjmJFzAD/7be12949284e184fee0c35ca2bd8dedb/web-margin_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1270px) and (max-width: 1859px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/GUCBY2ITkAgErQjmJFzAD/7be12949284e184fee0c35ca2bd8dedb/web-margin_trading-realized_PnL_details.png"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/GUCBY2ITkAgErQjmJFzAD/7be12949284e184fee0c35ca2bd8dedb/web-margin_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1269px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/GUCBY2ITkAgErQjmJFzAD/7be12949284e184fee0c35ca2bd8dedb/web-margin_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_976,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/GUCBY2ITkAgErQjmJFzAD/7be12949284e184fee0c35ca2bd8dedb/web-margin_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(min-width: 768px) and (max-width: 1023px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/GUCBY2ITkAgErQjmJFzAD/7be12949284e184fee0c35ca2bd8dedb/web-margin_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_696,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/GUCBY2ITkAgErQjmJFzAD/7be12949284e184fee0c35ca2bd8dedb/web-margin_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-media" media="(max-width: 767px)" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/GUCBY2ITkAgErQjmJFzAD/7be12949284e184fee0c35ca2bd8dedb/web-margin_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_736,type_6/ignore-error,1"/><source data-testid="okd-image-source-webp-default" srcSet="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/GUCBY2ITkAgErQjmJFzAD/7be12949284e184fee0c35ca2bd8dedb/web-margin_trading-realized_PnL_details.png?x-oss-process=image/format,webp/ignore-error,1"/><img data-testid="okd-picture-img-default" width="1600" height="200" class="index_baseImage__bDDyg" src="//www.okx.com/cdn/assets/plugins/announcements/contentful/tofttmniq0qv/GUCBY2ITkAgErQjmJFzAD/7be12949284e184fee0c35ca2bd8dedb/web-margin_trading-realized_PnL_details.png" alt="CT-web-margin trading-realized PnL details"/></picture></button></figure><p class="caption"><i>Find the explanation of the PnL for margin trading by hovering over the PnL field in your position history</i></p><h2 id="20-why-dont-my-trading-bots-profit-figures-match-my-trade-history">20. Why don&#x27;t my trading bot&#x27;s profit figures match my trade history?</h2><p>A trading bot reports profit using its own accounting, while your trade history and API export record each individual fill and the realized profit or loss on it. Your trade history and API export are the records of what was actually executed on your account, and they&#x27;re the data to use for your own reporting. Stopping or deleting a bot doesn&#x27;t change trade history or API data that has already been recorded.</p><h2 id="21-where-can-i-see-my-fee-tier-and-30-day-trading-volume-when-do-they-update">21. Where can I see my fee tier and 30-day trading volume? When do they update?</h2><p>Your trading fee rate is determined by your fee tier, which is based on your 30-day trading volume and your account asset holdings.<b>To check your fee tier:</b></p><ul><li><p><b>On the app</b>: select the <b>main menu</b> &gt;<b> profile picture</b> &gt; <b>User Center &gt;</b> <b>Account Information &gt;</b> <b>Trading fee tier</b></p></li><li><p><b>On the web</b>: select <b>Assets</b> &gt; <b>My trading fees</b></p></li></ul><p><b>How your tier updates:</b></p><ul><li><p>The platform takes a daily snapshot of your trading volume and your holdings of each currency at 0:00 (UTC+8)</p></li><li><p>Fee tiers are updated daily between 4:00 AM and 6:00 AM (UTC+8)</p></li><li><p>Tiers aren&#x27;t updated in real time. If your trading volume already meets the threshold, your tier is upgraded automatically once the update runs — you don&#x27;t need to do anything else.</p></li></ul><p><b>How trading volume is calculated:</b></p><ul><li><p>Daily trading volume (USD) = quantity of the asset traded that day × that day&#x27;s closing price of the asset (USDT) × that day&#x27;s USDT/USD closing price</p></li><li><p>Counted: spot, margin, futures/perpetual, options, and Convert. For example, XAUT/USDT margin trading counts toward spot volume, and the USDC/USDT perpetual counts toward futures volume.</p></li><li><p>Not counted: P2P trading, and the PYUSD/USDT, USDC/USDT, RLUSD/USDT, and USDG/USDT spot pairs</p></li><li><p>The platform only provides 30-day trading volume statistics. Longer periods aren&#x27;t available.</p></li></ul><h2 id="22-can-i-use-okb-holdings-to-offset-trading-fees">22. Can I use OKB holdings to offset trading fees?</h2><p>The platform currently doesn&#x27;t offer a feature that lets you offset trading fees by holding OKB. OKB is charged under the same standard fee rules as any other currency.</p><h2 id="23-is-there-a-fee-for-adjusting-leverage-or-adding-or-removing-margin-in-isolated-mode">23. Is there a fee for adjusting leverage or adding or removing margin in isolated mode?</h2><p>No. Adjusting your leverage, adding margin, or removing margin doesn&#x27;t incur any fee on its own.Trading fees are only charged when an order actually fills.</p><h2 id="24-if-i-just-hold-crypto-in-my-account-without-trading-am-i-charged-a-daily-fee">24. If I just hold crypto in my account without trading, am I charged a daily fee?</h2><p>No. For spot and margin trading, fees are charged only when a buy or sell order fills. Unfilled portions, cancelled orders, and simply holding assets don&#x27;t incur any fee.</p><p><b>Note:</b> perpetual futures positions incur a funding fee at each settlement point, but funding fees aren&#x27;t trading fees.</p><h2 id="25-is-the-funding-fee-a-trading-fee">25. Is the funding fee a trading fee?</h2><p>A funding fee isn&#x27;t a trading fee — they&#x27;re two different charges:</p><ul><li><p>Funding fees are settled between long and short traders, and the platform doesn&#x27;t take any cut</p></li><li><p>When the funding rate is positive, longs pay shorts. When it&#x27;s negative, shorts pay longs.</p></li><li><p>Settlement frequency varies by currency (every 8, 4, 2, or 1 hour). You can see the current rate and the countdown to the next settlement above the order book.</p></li><li><p>Funding is only settled if you hold a position at the settlement point. If you close your position before the countdown ends, you aren&#x27;t part of that settlement.</p></li><li><p>Formula: funding fee = position value × funding rate</p><ul><li><p>USDT-margined position value = contract face value × number of contracts × mark price</p></li><li><p>Crypto-margined position value = contract face value × number of contracts ÷ mark price</p></li></ul></li></ul><p><b>Note:</b> if your available balance isn&#x27;t enough to cover the funding fee, the system deducts it from your position margin, which pushes your liquidation price up and increases liquidation risk. We recommend keeping a sufficient available balance while you hold positions.</p><h2 id="26-whats-the-face-value-in-the-fee-formula-how-does-the-number-of-contracts-relate-to-the-position-size-i-see">26. What&#x27;s the &quot;face value&quot; in the fee formula? How does the number of contracts relate to the position size I see?</h2><ul><li><p>Face value is the value of the underlying asset represented by one contract. It&#x27;s fixed and differs for each currency. For example, the BTC-USDT perpetual has a face value of 0.01 BTC.</p></li><li><p>Face value × number of contracts = position size. For example, if the page shows a position size of 1.0935 BTC, that corresponds to 109.35 contracts (0.01 × 109.35 = 1.0935).</p></li><li><p>To check the face value of a specific contract, select the three dots at the top-right of the trading page &gt; <b>Market information</b></p></li></ul><p>So &quot;face value × number of contracts × fill price&quot; in the fee formula is the actual value of that fill. Fees are calculated on fill value and have no direct relationship to your leverage — Leverage only affects how large a position you can open.</p><h2 id="27-i-only-placed-one-order--why-does-it-show-multiple-fills-was-i-overcharged">27. I only placed one order — why does it show multiple fills? Was I overcharged?</h2><p>You weren&#x27;t overcharged. A single order may fill in parts against multiple counterparties in the market, and the order details page lists each of those fills individually.Fees are calculated separately for each fill and then totalled. The total is the same as it would be for a single fill — nothing is charged twice. No fee is charged on the unfilled portion.</p><h2 id="28-can-trading-fees-that-have-already-been-charged-be-refunded">28. Can trading fees that have already been charged be refunded?</h2><p>Trading fees generated by filled orders aren&#x27;t refundable. Fees are a cost to factor in when trading, and the platform charges them under publicly disclosed, transparent rules.</p><h2 id="29-are-there-fees-on-p2p-trades-do-they-count-toward-trading-volume">29. Are there fees on P2P trades? Do they count toward trading volume?</h2><p>P2P buy and sell transactions aren&#x27;t charged a trading fee.</p><p><b>Note:</b> P2P trades don&#x27;t count toward your 30-day trading volume, so they don&#x27;t affect your fee tier. They also don&#x27;t count toward the &quot;eligible trading volume&quot; thresholds used in the platform&#x27;s various campaigns.</p><h2 id="30why-dont-the-fee-rates-and-borrowing-limits-i-see-when-im-logged-out-match-my-account">30.Why don&#x27;t the fee rates and borrowing limits I see when I&#x27;m logged out match my account?</h2><p>Rates, fee tiers, and maximum borrowing limits shown to a logged-out visitor are published reference figures. They aren&#x27;t tied to any account, so they can differ from the figures that apply to you.Log in first, then check your own figures:</p><ul><li><p>Trading fees and fee tier: <span class="okui-hyperlink-var okui-hyperlink okui-hyperlink-accent okui-hyperlink-underline okui-hyperlink-md okui-hyperlink-muted index_hyperlink__f2YQn" data-testid="okd-hyperlink"><a href="/en-us/balance/fee" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_self" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-hyperlink-text index_mutedLink__UPRKk">My trading fees</a></span>, or the <span class="okui-hyperlink-var okui-hyperlink okui-hyperlink-accent okui-hyperlink-underline okui-hyperlink-md okui-hyperlink-muted index_hyperlink__f2YQn" data-testid="okd-hyperlink"><a href="/en-us/fees" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_self" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-hyperlink-text index_mutedLink__UPRKk">fee schedule</a></span></p></li><li><p>Margin interest rates and maximum borrowing limits: <span class="okui-hyperlink-var okui-hyperlink okui-hyperlink-accent okui-hyperlink-underline okui-hyperlink-md okui-hyperlink-muted index_hyperlink__f2YQn" data-testid="okd-hyperlink"><a href="/en-us/fees/margin" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_self" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-hyperlink-text index_mutedLink__UPRKk">Margin interest rate</a></span></p></li></ul><p>The fee tier, rates, and borrowing limits shown on those pages once you&#x27;re logged in are the ones that apply to your account. If a figure you saw before logging in doesn&#x27;t match, treat the logged-in figures as the ones that apply.</p><p></p></div></div></div><!--$--><div class="index_articleSidebarContainer__6J-mn"><div class="index_inner__Ie1xc"><nav class="index_outlineContainer__x5BS0" aria-label="Article"><ul><li id="article-nav-active" class="index_headingItem__NxzcE index_active__ic4-F" aria-current="page"><a href="#1-when-will-the-maker-and-taker-fees-occur-what-is-the-difference-between-maker-and-taker-fees" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>1. When will the maker and taker fees occur? What is the difference between maker and taker fees?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#2-why-are-the-fees-different-for-market-orders-and-limit-orders" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>2. Why are the fees different for market orders and limit orders?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#3-how-do-i-check-my-current-trading-fee-rate-what-are-the-fee-rates-and-commissions-for-each-vip-level" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>3. How do I check my current trading fee rate? What are the fee rates and commissions for each VIP level?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#4-how-do-i-check-the-current-fee-rate-for-a-specific-pair-on-the-trading-page" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>4. How do I check the current fee rate for a specific pair on the trading page?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#5-how-can-i-check-the-trading-fees-in-advance" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>5. How can I check the trading fees in advance?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#6-how-are-trading-fees-paid-can-i-pay-them-separately" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>6. How are trading fees paid? Can I pay them separately?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#7-why-is-the-amount-i-received-different-from-what-i-expected-is-the-spread-a-hidden-fee" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>7. Why is the amount I received different from what I expected? Is the spread a hidden fee?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#8-does-okx-charge-any-other-trading-fees" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>8. Does OKX charge any other trading fees?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#9-is-there-a-daily-limit-on-how-much-i-can-trade" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>9. Is there a daily limit on how much I can trade?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#10-how-can-i-upgrade-my-vip-level-and-reduce-trading-fees" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>10. How can I upgrade my VIP level and reduce trading fees?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#11-how-do-i-view-the-total-trading-fees-for-futures" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>11. How do I view the total trading fees for Futures?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#12-how-do-i-view-the-total-profitloss-for-futures" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>12. How do I view the total profit/loss for Futures?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#13-how-do-i-check-the-fees-for-my-historical-orders" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>13. How do I check the fees for my historical orders?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#14-how-is-my-trading-fee-level-determined" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>14. How is my trading fee level determined?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#15-how-is-the-trading-fee-calculated" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>15. How is the trading fee calculated?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#16-whats-the-difference-between-futures-opening-and-closing-fees" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>16. What’s the difference between futures opening and closing fees?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#17-are-fees-charged-for-liquidation" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>17. Are fees charged for liquidation?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#18-why-is-there-a-discrepancy-between-the-profit-when-holding-a-position-and-after-closing-it" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>18. Why is there a discrepancy between the profit when holding a position and after closing it?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#19-why-are-the-profits-from-order-history-and-position-history-inconsistent" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>19. Why are the profits from Order history and Position history inconsistent?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#20-why-dont-my-trading-bots-profit-figures-match-my-trade-history" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>20. Why don&#x27;t my trading bot&#x27;s profit figures match my trade history?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#21-where-can-i-see-my-fee-tier-and-30-day-trading-volume-when-do-they-update" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>21. Where can I see my fee tier and 30-day trading volume? When do they update?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#22-can-i-use-okb-holdings-to-offset-trading-fees" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>22. Can I use OKB holdings to offset trading fees?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#23-is-there-a-fee-for-adjusting-leverage-or-adding-or-removing-margin-in-isolated-mode" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>23. Is there a fee for adjusting leverage or adding or removing margin in isolated mode?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#24-if-i-just-hold-crypto-in-my-account-without-trading-am-i-charged-a-daily-fee" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>24. If I just hold crypto in my account without trading, am I charged a daily fee?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#25-is-the-funding-fee-a-trading-fee" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>25. Is the funding fee a trading fee?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#26-whats-the-face-value-in-the-fee-formula-how-does-the-number-of-contracts-relate-to-the-position-size-i-see" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>26. What&#x27;s the &quot;face value&quot; in the fee formula? How does the number of contracts relate to the position size I see?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#27-i-only-placed-one-order--why-does-it-show-multiple-fills-was-i-overcharged" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>27. I only placed one order — why does it show multiple fills? Was I overcharged?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#28-can-trading-fees-that-have-already-been-charged-be-refunded" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>28. Can trading fees that have already been charged be refunded?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#29-are-there-fees-on-p2p-trades-do-they-count-toward-trading-volume" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>29. Are there fees on P2P trades? Do they count toward trading volume?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li><li class="index_headingItem__NxzcE"><a href="#30why-dont-the-fee-rates-and-borrowing-limits-i-see-when-im-logged-out-match-my-account" rel="noopener" class="okui-powerLink-a11y okui-powerLink"><span>30.Why don&#x27;t the fee rates and borrowing limits I see when I&#x27;m logged out match my account?</span><div class="index_border__t4yCV"></div></a></li></ul></nav></div></div><!--/$--></div></article></div><div id="article-overlay" class="index_stickyRegion__VKIJu"></div></div>
      <script data-id="__app_data_for_ssr__" type="application/json" id="appState">{"appContext":{"initialProps":{"supportBanner":{"text":"Not all products mentioned are available in all jurisdictions."},"articleLikes":{"likes":1101},"content":{"headings":[{"id":"1-when-will-the-maker-and-taker-fees-occur-what-is-the-difference-between-maker-and-taker-fees","title":"1. When will the maker and taker fees occur? What is the difference between maker and taker fees?","level":2},{"id":"2-why-are-the-fees-different-for-market-orders-and-limit-orders","title":"2. Why are the fees different for market orders and limit orders?","level":2},{"id":"3-how-do-i-check-my-current-trading-fee-rate-what-are-the-fee-rates-and-commissions-for-each-vip-level","title":"3. How do I check my current trading fee rate? What are the fee rates and commissions for each VIP level?","level":2},{"id":"4-how-do-i-check-the-current-fee-rate-for-a-specific-pair-on-the-trading-page","title":"4. How do I check the current fee rate for a specific pair on the trading page?","level":2},{"id":"5-how-can-i-check-the-trading-fees-in-advance","title":"5. How can I check the trading fees in advance?","level":2},{"id":"6-how-are-trading-fees-paid-can-i-pay-them-separately","title":"6. How are trading fees paid? Can I pay them separately?","level":2},{"id":"7-why-is-the-amount-i-received-different-from-what-i-expected-is-the-spread-a-hidden-fee","title":"7. Why is the amount I received different from what I expected? Is the spread a hidden fee?","level":2},{"id":"8-does-okx-charge-any-other-trading-fees","title":"8. Does OKX charge any other trading fees?","level":2},{"id":"9-is-there-a-daily-limit-on-how-much-i-can-trade","title":"9. Is there a daily limit on how much I can trade?","level":2},{"id":"10-how-can-i-upgrade-my-vip-level-and-reduce-trading-fees","title":"10. How can I upgrade my VIP level and reduce trading fees?","level":2},{"id":"11-how-do-i-view-the-total-trading-fees-for-futures","title":"11. Ho